    {
      "id": "readme",
      "type": "note",
      "name": "README.txt",
      "parent": "desktop",
      "date": "2009-03-21",
      "text": "FOUND DESKTOP\n=============\n\nThis computer was bought secondhand in 2009.\nNobody wiped the hard drive.\n\nThese are the files that were left on the desktop:\nphotos named by a camera instead of a person,\na few notes, and one folder someone started\nand never finished.\n\nYou can't know what these pictures meant to\nthe person who took them. But you can decide\nwhat they mean now.\n\n  - drag files into folders, or into piles anywhere\n  - right-click the desktop to make a new folder,\n    or to arrange everything by date (a timeline)\n  - double-click to open, F2 to rename,\n    Delete to throw something away\n  - Start > Search to find things by name or year\n  - drag your own pictures onto the screen\n    to leave something behind\n\nWhatever order you give them becomes their story."
    },
